     "page": 1,
     "text": "FAX 13  -- ROI --\n**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Klein Ingram and Joyce Clinic** \n**Patient:** Lisa Rose \n**DOB:** 12/03/1995 \n**Sex:** F \n**MRN:** 705565 \n\n**Encounters:** \n- **2026-04-14:** Breast cancer, stage I; BP 128/90; Wt 182 lbs \n- **2025-07-08:** Breast cancer, stage I; BP 123/96; Wt 170 lbs \n- **2024-10-01:** Lab review; 122/89; Wt 166 lbs \n- **2023-12-26:** Breast cancer, stage I; BP 131/92; Wt 182 lbs \n\n**Assessment/Plan:** \n- **Breast Cancer, Stage I (s/p treatment ~10.7 years ago) - Controlled; Meds: None** \n Lisa Rose has been under consistent surveillance for her stage I breast cancer, which she underwent treatment for approximately 10.7 years ago. As of the most recent assessment, the cancer remains controlled, with no evidence of recurrence or metastasis. She has not been prescribed any medications for this condition. \n- **Patient Non-Compliant with Medications** \n The patient has been non-compliant with her medication regimen, and she has missed two follow-up appointments. This could potentially impact her ongoing management and monitoring for breast cancer. \n- **Vitals:** \n Recent vital signs have shown blood pressures within acceptable ranges and weight fluctuations which are being monitored. \n - **2026-04-14:** BP 128/90; Wt 182 lbs \n - **2025-07-08:** BP 123/96; Wt 170 lbs \n - **2024-10-01:** BP 122/89; Wt 166 lbs \n - **2023-12-26:** BP 131/92; Wt 182 lbs \n- **Social History:** \n - **Tobacco Use:** Lisa had a history of smoking cigarettes, approximately half a pack per day, starting from January 24, 2012. She successfully quit smoking on November 3, 2024, and has been tobacco-free since then. \n - **Alcohol Use:** She consumes alcohol on an average of three days per week, with approximately three drinks each occasion. \n\n**Exam Findings:** \nDuring the visits, the physical exams have been largely unremarkable with no significant abnormalities noted. Lisa's general physical condition and other systems (cardiovascular, respiratory, etc.) remain within normal limits. \n\n**Family History:** \nLisa's mother had a history of myocardial infarction (MI) at the age of 65 and passed away at 84 years old. \n\n**Additional Notes:** \n- The patient has been under our care for continuous monitoring of her breast cancer status.\n- Lisa has shown some challenges with adherence to her medication schedule and follow-up appointments, which is being addressed through additional patient education and support.\n- The patient reports no significant new complaints and continues to maintain a generally healthy lifestyle"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": ". \n\n**Conclusion:** \nLisa Rose’s stage I breast cancer remains controlled, and she is closely monitored for any signs of recurrence. Her overall health status is stable with no new concerning symptoms. Continued vigilance and adherence to follow-up care are recommended to maintain her current health status.\n"
    }
